        "summary": "The geometry course page was tested for interactivity and content. \n\n**Key Findings:**\n1. **Critical Failure:** The 'Interactive Activity' section contains placeholder text: \"Interactive content will be placed here (quizzes, exercises, interactive games, etc.)\". Per the instructions, this is a major issue as the interactive content is missing.\n2. **Navigation:** 'Previous' and 'Next' buttons are present. Since the page indicates '1 of 1' modules, the 'Next' button does not navigate to a new page.\n3. **Notes Tool:** The notes button successfully opens a panel. I verified that the text area accepts input.\n4. **Chatbot:** The chatbot toggle works, and the input field/send button respond to interaction.\n5. **Audio Controls:** Numerous audio buttons are placed next to content sections (Video, Explanation, Key Points, Timeline, etc.).\n6. **Content:** The page includes a video placeholder, a text explanation, key points, and a historical timeline.\n\n**Conclusion:** While the UI shell and auxiliary tools (notes, chatbot) are functional, the core requirement of an 'interactive geometry course' is failed due to the placeholder text in the interactive activity section."
